# Root .dockerignore — applies to every `docker build` rooted at the repo.
# Keeps the build context small (faster transfers, smaller layer cache).
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT exclude dev/retro/. The deploy/retro/* Dockerfiles use
# the repo root as their build context and need to COPY from dev/retro/
# (Holo5 submodules + SQL dumps).

# ── Dependencies (will be installed inside the image) ────────────
**/node_modules
**/.pnp
**/.pnp.js

# ── Build outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.nx
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Environment / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ── VCS / CI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# ── Editor / OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log

# ── Local-dev / scratch directories that shouldn't ship ──────────
**/tmp
**/.turbo

# ── The Cypress binary (huge; tests don't run inside the image) ──
**/cypress/screenshots
**/cypress/videos
**/cypress/downloads

# ── Docs we don't need at build time ─────────────────────────────
**/*.md
!README.md
